WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.713
Here are the three gates on one page,
so you know where this is going.

2
00:00:03.713 --> 00:00:09.312
Gate 7 is done when one personnel action
changes access only through the attributes.

3
00:00:09.312 --> 00:00:12.724
Gate 8 is done when every
population has cut over

4
00:00:12.724 --> 00:00:16.137
by query and nothing reads
OU placement any more.

5
00:00:16.137 --> 00:00:20.460
Gate 9 is done when drift scans
run, findings close at the source,

6
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.037
and the nightly plan has nothing to do.

7
00:00:23.037 --> 00:00:24.988
The CISO owns all three.

8
00:00:24.988 --> 00:00:28.763
Watch the schedule, because this
is where the critical path lives.

9
00:00:28.763 --> 00:00:31.987
From the program's G3 in
week 36 there's no float:

10
00:00:31.987 --> 00:00:37.674
the transitional sync rules come out, the
tree freezes after the OU groups retire,

11
00:00:37.674 --> 00:00:41.324
and the last drift cycle
closes both gates in week 40.

12
00:00:41.324 --> 00:00:46.580
Our running example is the same budget
analyst, keyed by an existing enterprise ID.
